            <article>
                <div class="tn-pagetitle show" aria-hidden="false">
    <h1>Grants Administration</h1>
    

</div>

                <div>




    
    
    <div class="tn-cta parbase">
    <a href="/environment/program-areas/solid-waste.html" class="text-button icon-right-1" alt="Materials Management Program Main Page">Materials Management Program Main Page</a>


</div>


    
    
    <div class="tn-cta parbase">
    <a href="/environment/program-areas/solid-waste.html" class="text-button icon-right-1" alt="Waste Management Branch Main Page">Waste Management Branch Main Page</a>


</div>


    
    
    <div class="tn-rte">
    
        <h2>Solid Waste Grants</h2>
<p>The Tennessee Department of Environment and Conservation (TDEC), Division of Land Protection - Waste Management Branch (DLP-WMB), Materials Management Program Grants Administration, provides grant funding opportunities to municipalities, counties, and nonprofits throughout the State. This funding provides critical infrastructure, equipment, and education to help meet solid waste, recycling, and waste reduction goals for the Solid Waste Management Plan (SWP). TDEC is dedicated to assisting the state in improving recycling and reducing waste being deposited into landfills.</p>
<p>The following grants are currently closed to applications.</p>
<ul><li><a href="/content/tn/environment/about-tdec/grants/materials-management/technical-assistance.html" title="Link to Technical Assistance Grant page"><span class="icon-link-ext"></span>Technical Assistance Grant</a> </li><li><a href="/content/tn/environment/about-tdec/grants/materials-management/organics-management.html" title="Link to Organics webpage"><span class="icon-link-ext"></span>Organics Management Grant</a></li><li><a href="/content/tn/environment/about-tdec/grants/materials-management/convenience-center.html" title="Link Convenience Center Grant webpage"><span class="icon-link-ext"></span>Convenience Center Grant</a></li><li><a href="/content/tn/environment/about-tdec/grants/materials-management/used-oil.html" title="Link to used oil grant"><span class="icon-link-ext"></span>Used Automotive Recycling Fluid Grant</a></li><li><a href="/content/tn/environment/about-tdec/grants/materials-management/recycling-equipment.html" title="Link to Recycling Euipment grant webpage"><span class="icon-link-ext"></span>Recycling Equipment Grant</a></li><li><a href="/content/tn/environment/about-tdec/grants/materials-management/hhw-collection-facility.html" target="_blank" title="Link to HHW Grant webpage" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong><span class="icon-link-ext"></span></strong>Household Hazardous Waste Grant</a></li><li><a href="/content/tn/environment/about-tdec/grants/materials-management/recycling-rebate.html" target="_blank" title="Link to Recycling Rebate webpage" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong><span class="icon-link-ext"></span></strong>Recycling Rebate</a></li></ul>
<h2><span style="	letter-spacing: -0.075em;
">Grants Management System </span></h2>
<p>If you are interested in applying for available grants, please visit the <span class="icon-link-ext"></span><a href="https://tdec.smartsimple.com/s_Login.jsp" target="_blank" title="Grants Management System" rel="noopener noreferrer">Grants Management System</a>.</p>
<h2>Grants Awarded FY24</h2>
<p>The Division of Land Protection Grants Administration Program awarded over seven million dollars for the following  for FY26 grants:</p>
<ul><li><strong>FY26 Grants Awarded Totaling $8,674,066</strong><ul><li>(18) $4,509,340 - Waste Reduction</li><li>(5) $403,563 - Organics Management</li><li>(8) $651,580 – Technical Assistance for Development Districts</li><li>(9) $1,071,577 – Convenience Center</li><li>(6) $150,804 – Used Automotive Fluid Recycling (Used Oil)</li><li>(9) $1,038,630 - Recycling Equipment Grant</li><li>(8) $726,072- Recycling Rebates</li><li>(2) $122,500 - Household Hazardous Waste</li></ul>
</li></ul>
<p><strong>If your region, county, or municipality is interested in these upcoming opportunities, please contact your local technical assistance providers or planners to begin discussions.</strong> Please note that the dates referenced above are not established but are tentative dates of application. Please continue to access the Grants Management System (GMS) online portal for the most up-to-date information.</p>
<p>Unofficial draft manuals are available on request. Be aware that these manuals are subject to edit or update until the date of the application becoming open for submission in the GMS portal.</p>
<p>Our deepest appreciation goes out to all of our organizations, regions, counties, and municipalities for their dedication to the preservation of our environment and the beauty of our State. We look forward to continuing to accomplish the goals of waste reduction and increased recycling across Tennessee.<br />
</p>

    
    

</div>


    
    
